.TH GIT-CONTRIB 1 2026-11-11 "git-contributions" "Git Manual"
.SH NAME
git-contrib \- measure authors' contributions to a LaTeX project kept in Git
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B git contrib
.I subcommand
.RI [ options ]
.br
.B git contrib
.B \-h
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B git contrib
follows every word of a LaTeX project (a book, an article, a paper) through the history
of its Git repository and finds out who wrote it, word by word rather than line by line (a
line of LaTeX source is often a whole paragraph).
It never modifies the measured repository: the history is rewritten in a copy, in a
sibling directory named
.IR repo \fB\-\-contrib\-\-\fR ref \- hash ,
which is kept and reused by later runs.
Each subcommand writes its report to a file and prints its progress, the file name and
the time taken on standard error.
.SH SUBCOMMANDS
.TP
.B shares
Every author's fair share of the project, in percent: writing counts most, rewriting someone
else's text less, moving text little, and a draft someone else replaced half.
.TP
.B profile
One author's contribution measured in many ways (words, uncommon words, sentences,
formulas, paragraphs), with a fair and a maximal estimate.
.TP
.B surviving
Everything one author wrote that is still in the project, sentence by sentence.
.TP
.B removed
Everything one author wrote that was later deleted or replaced, commit by commit.
.TP
.B highlight
The whole project as one LaTeX file with one author's words highlighted.
.SH OPTIONS
Every subcommand accepts these options; run
.B git contrib
.I subcommand
.B \-\-help
for the rest.
.TP
.BI \-\-repo " dir"
The measured repository (default: the one containing the current directory).
.TP
.BI \-\-main " file"
The main
.B .tex
file, relative to the repository root (default: the value of
.BR "git config contrib.main" ).
.TP
.BI \-\-commit " rev"
The branch, tag or commit to measure (default:
.BR HEAD ).
.TP
.BI \-\-author " regex"
The author, for every subcommand but
.BR shares :
a case-insensitive regular expression matched against
.I Name <email>
of every commit, as recorded and after
.BR .mailmap .
.TP
.BI \-\-format " format"
.BR json ,
.B markdown
or
.B latex
(default:
.BR markdown ;
not for
.BR highlight ).
.TP
.BI \-\-output " file"
The report (default: a name built from the subcommand, the author and the revision, in
the current directory).
.SH CONFIGURATION
.TP
.B contrib.main
The main file, so that
.B \-\-main
can be left out:
.B git config contrib.main main.tex
in the project's repository.
.SH NOTES
.B git contrib
works in the current directory and with
.B git \-C
.IR dir ,
but not with
.B git \-\-git\-dir
or
.BR \-\-work\-tree :
it removes every
.B GIT_*
environment variable before running git, so that git can never be pointed at the measured
repository by accident, and refuses to run when those two are set.
.PP
A subcommand given no options at all runs with all defaults; one-author subcommands
still need
.BR \-\-author .
.PP
.B git contrib \-\-help
shows this page;
.B git contrib \-h
lists the subcommands.
.SH EXAMPLES
.nf
git config contrib.main main.tex
git contrib shares
git contrib profile \-\-author 'kowalski' \-\-format latex
git contrib highlight \-\-author 'kowalski' \-\-commit v1.0
.fi
.SH SEE ALSO
The documentation of each subcommand in the
.B docs
directory of the scripts:
.BR author_shares.md ,
.BR author_profile.md ,
.BR surviving_text.md ,
.BR removed_text.md ,
.BR highlight_author.md ,
and
.BR git-contrib.md .
